# Rust build output. Cargo.lock IS committed — deCPLD ships binaries
# (`decpld`, `decpld-lsp`) and CI builds with `--locked`.
/target/
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
*.iml

# Compiler output from in-tree dev runs. Generated JEDEC belongs in a
# build directory, never next to the source it came from. Fixture and
# evidence `.jed` files under `targets/` are checked in deliberately and
# are not matched by these paths.
/build/
/out/

# WinCUPL oracle installation and run artifacts (SPEC.md Part VII).
# WinCUPL is proprietary: its executables, device libraries, and any
# embedded serial numbers must never be redistributed from this repo.
# Only the *derived, normalized* fixtures under `targets/fixtures/` are
# committed, and only where licensing permits.
/tools/wincupl/install/
/tools/wincupl/prefix/
/tools/wincupl/**/*.exe
/tools/wincupl/**/*.dl
/oracle-runs/

# Local agent worktrees: each is a live `git worktree add` into a
# sibling branch, not source. Without this entry, `git add -A` from the
# main checkout greedily slurps every worktree directory as a gitlink,
# polluting commits with cross-session worktree state.
.claude/worktrees/

# Claude Code local state — machine-specific settings and task locks.
# The shared, committed config is `.claude/skills/` and CLAUDE.md.
/.claude/settings*.json
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Third-party reference documents. `targets/evidence/references.toml`
# records each one's URL and sha256; the documents are copyrighted and
# are re-fetched on demand by `targets/evidence/verify-references.sh`,
# never committed. The manifest, README, and script are tracked.
/targets/evidence/*
!/targets/evidence/README.md
!/targets/evidence/references.toml
!/targets/evidence/verify-references.sh

# Logs and scratch
*.log
scratch/
tmp/
